From 6d9bcacae6e1cc0fdcc9fd8ad95f0e98666fc6b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Belkin <anton.belkin@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:29:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mac/vulkan: measure each frame for its Dolby Vision L1

With --macos-dovi-live-l1, each frame the sample buffer layer presents
is measured on the GPU (a Metal kernel over the buffer macOS gets,
inside the video's rectangle): the lowest, average and highest
max(R,G,B) in PQ, HLG taken to PQ for a 1000-nit display as a profile
8.4 RPU maps it. That goes into the L1 of the RPU --macos-dovi-rpu-file
gives the frame (clamped as dovi_tool's generator clamps L1, the CRC
written anew), so macOS's display management maps each frame for what
is in it instead of for the file's fixed values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
