+``--macos-dovi-live-l1=<yes|no>``
+    Measure each frame ``--macos-sample-buffer-layer`` presents and write what it found into the L1 of
+    the RPU from ``--macos-dovi-rpu-file`` (default: no): the lowest, average and highest max(R,G,B) of
+    the video's pixels in PQ (HLG taken to PQ for a 1000-nit display, as a profile 8.4 RPU maps it),
+    clamped as ``dovi_tool generate`` clamps L1. macOS's Dolby Vision display management then maps each
+    frame for what's in it instead of for the file's fixed values. Measured on the GPU, on the buffer
+    macOS gets; frames with their own RPU keep it. Can be changed while playing.
+
